Base: p3s2_conform.py at exopipe_ops 074f96c (md5 7504f11a78f445a097d0c57c5fad193d); patched md5 6d592cf8f4e548cd65f5b306b8c34cdb.

THE DECISION. Production's conformance removes a row whose catalog |S/N| > 8 and normalized axis ratio > 2.0 x the epoch beam's.
The step came from R-AXIS-RATIO-REMOVAL-ABOVE-8SIGMA (Gregg 2026-09-05: "Approved - remove above 8 sigma local SNR when the
normalized axis ratio exceeds 2.0; flag 1.5 to 2.0; no action below 8 sigma"). R-SIZE-AXIS-GATE-1.5-RATIFIED (2026-09-09: "1.5
and 1.5 is correct and should run from now on!"; ledger: "Supersedes ... the 2.0 axis value of R-AXIS-RATIO-REMOVAL-ABOVE-8SIGMA")
superseded that 2.0 value; the conformance's 2.0 step has stood since only in production's code, inert behind the search's 1.5.
R-GREGG-20261022-ALL-APPROVED-SIZE-GATE-READMISSION-SUBAGENTS: the rule at every S/N "replaces the fixed thresholds (1.5 / 1.5
above 8 sigma; 1.7 at 7-8 sigma for unpromoted singles)" - it did not name the conformance's step. Under the rule the search keeps
axis ratios up to max(1.5, the 99th percentile of injected point sources): 3.92 for deep I low bands at S/N 8, 3.05 at 9, 2.27
at 10; 3.34 for 10-minute I low bands at 8. So the 2.0 step acts again on the rule's attempts. Gregg 2026-11-04
(R-GREGG-20261104-AXIS-THRESHOLD-DECIDE-FROM-PULSARS): "You should decide, based on the data (e.g. verified pulsars again) what is
the correct threshold to use!" The refactor chat decided (R-REFACTOR-20261104-AXIS-RULE-ALONE-FULLBAND-SIZE-OFF-FROM-PULSARS): the
calibrated rule alone, this step retired. On 9 verified isolated pulsars the 2.0 step on top of the rule removes 0.3% [0.1, 1.1]
(deep) and 0.1% [0.0, 0.6] (10-minute) of the Stokes I detections above 8 sigma, and the pulsars' 99th-percentile axis ratio lies
inside the envelope in every S/N bin; the rows the step alone would remove (4,946 deep, 5,400 10-minute) lie mostly at cataloged
bright sources, for the later gates; their effect on the served catalogs is measured at the first full refactor run
(refactor_analysis/review_items_20261031/axis_pulsars_20261104/AXIS_PULSARS_20261104.md).

WHERE THE REFACTOR RUNS THIS SCRIPT ON ATTEMPTS SEARCHED UNDER THE RULE (each gets P3_CONFORM_AXIS=0 under 'replace'):
  - 10-minute S-G13 conformance (lib/catalog/tier_sublst.st_conform) - every LST;
  - the deep multiples fork, a mandatory stage of every deep pass but P3T* (exopipe_ops/multiples_fork.py: its validity
    conformance runs this script in place - fork mode, table off - on the chain's finals plus its table-cut rows at |S/N| >= 7
    (I) / 5 (V); its conform() builds the child's environment from os.environ, so the switch reaches every run: validity A, table
    B / B2, the members' and calibration runs). The deep catalog therefore depends on this switch as much as the 10-minute
    one, although the deep main conformance itself is the refactor's check (lib/catalog/conform_check, MODE 'check');
  - deep MODE 'remove' and the incremental replay (production paths; the parity file).
Until this patch is in exopipe_ops, 'replace' REFUSES before any of those stages runs (lib/search/size_rule.conform_axis_refusal:
the script must read os.environ.get('P3_CONFORM_AXIS', '1')); 'second_gate' (production's behavior, the parity file's value) needs
no patch.

WHAT IT CHANGES. Unset or any value but '0' (every production pass): nothing - the same statements run in the same order
(AXIS_STEP is True: the new first branch never fires and the old second 'if' becomes an 'elif' after a 'continue'); byte-identical
outputs and printed lines (tests/test_removal_rules.py test_pending_patch, eight Run_P3S5 cells with axis ratios that fire).
P3_CONFORM_AXIS=0: a row above the 2.0 step is KEPT with axis_flag 'axis > 2.0 x beam (kept: point-like at its S/N by the size /
axis rule)' (counted n_akept, one extra printed line 'conform: axis-ratio step OFF ...' before the summary); the 1.5-2.0 flag and
every other step unchanged. The refactor's port (lib/search/removal_rules.conform) does the same under 'replace', word for word.

